"""Scientific TASK for joining compatible saved experimental components."""

COMPILED_ASSAY_TASK = """Evaluate what the selected experimental measurements establish about the studied molecule's measured activity and the functional assertion under investigation. Identify the actual molecule, construct, preparation, experimental system, endpoint, conditions and intended variable. Use source-supported context already available or examine the relevant source when needed. A function may emerge from the investigation; an initial candidate annotation is not required.

Select the saved numerical components that answer the assigned question. Establish each component's physical meaning, units, denominator and relationship to the particular assay. Matching names, units or publication do not establish applicability. Preserve the distinction between the directly measured endpoint and the asserted molecular function, including unresolved reporter-to-product relationships.

Determine which corrections have already been applied. Distinguish sample-minus-blank rate from gross signal, separately measured contamination from background already removed, instrument recovery from an enzyme-spike response, and total-molecule amount from active-site amount. Do not repeat subtraction, calibration or normalization already incorporated in a measurement. Preserve incompatible measurements as useful evidence while leaving the unsupported combined result unavailable.

Examine comparability outside the intended change and isolation of the measured effect separately. A condition-control response must address the relevant nuisance difference while excluding the variable deliberately tested. Establish whether compared molecules replace one another or coexist. Preserve additional changes, mixed contributors and alternative explanations rather than treating a control label as proof of isolation.

Preserve the underlying measurement owners and shared inputs across components. A calculated recovery ratio depends on its measured and nominal standards; a net optical rate can share background, calibration or path-length inputs with other results. Do not treat derived quantities as independent because they appear in different sections. Retain reported uncertainty and replication meanings; select covariance and a sampling model only when supported.

Nominate the applicable saved operands, experimental relationships and correction stages. Deterministic functions perform validation, unit conversion and arithmetic. Retain usable partial results when a relationship, measurement or required implementation is missing, and distinguish those reasons. Return only the requested numerical sections and their necessary qualifications. Do not invent missing controls, a universal quality grade, function probability, target-transfer weight or cross-assay total.

Assess uncertainty for the particular numerical result requested. Activity per molecular amount can have supported uncertainty even when additional contamination or condition corrections are unknown. Use the joint uncertainty of the actual operands, retaining shared measurements and signed covariance. Keep uncertainty propagated from those operands separate from additional residual variability. Do not invent missing corrections, assume missing covariance is zero, or present a partial result’s uncertainty as the uncertainty of a fully corrected activity."""

OPERATION_DESCRIPTION = "Compile the requested numerical sections of the studied molecule's experimental assessment. The original within-assay branches join actually received measurement, calibration, amount, nuisance-control and uncertainty cells under their applicable correction model. The explicit common-assessment branch compares received native product/cofactor and kinetic estimates with source-bound spectral binding parameters, substrate concentrations and named model assumptions; distinguish endpoint contrasts, conditional occupancy alternatives and applicable physical corrections. Select source-supported meanings and exact source spans rather than entering scientific values. Preserve shared measurements, original uncertainty meanings and unknown covariance. Return only requested numerical components and necessary qualifications; no universal reliability grade, target-transfer weight or annotation credit."


# The complete reviewed six-paragraph recurring comparison TASK.
COMMON_ASSESSMENT_TASK = "Determine what the selected experiments establish about the studied molecule's measured function and the particular comparison or alternative explanation under investigation. Start from supplied material and evidence actually received; a candidate annotation is not required. Identify the organism, constructs, preparations, experimental system, intended change and additional differences. Establish whether compared molecules replace one another or coexist.\n\nIdentify each endpoint and its functional resolution. Keep chemically identified product formation, reporter turnover, substrate binding, fitted saturation turnover and low-substrate efficiency distinct. Select measurements with their actual units, denominators, conditions and source locations. Preserve reported uncertainty, censoring and replication meanings. Do not borrow uncertainty or experimental conditions from a neighboring table or assay.\n\nEstablish which measurements can be compared and what the comparison evaluates. Examine comparability outside the intended change separately from isolation of the measured effect. Identify applicable background controls, recovery standards, active amounts and nuisance-response measurements. Retain missing or conflicting relationships; matching units, names or publication do not establish compatibility.\n\nFor a named alternative explanation, identify the physical model and its applicability. A binding-based occupancy comparison requires the relevant binding parameter, substrate concentration, free-versus-total treatment and relationship between binding and catalytic conditions. Distinguish supported assumptions from explicitly stipulated sensitivity scenarios. Preserve conditional calculations without presenting them as measured corrections or proof of the residual's cause.\n\nAsk deterministic readers and calculators for the requested numerical components. Preserve shared references, measurement reuse and covariance across contrasts. Different endpoints can address complementary weaknesses; they do not automatically provide independent replication. Compare disagreements only between compatible estimands or through an explicit connecting model. Unknown covariance remains unknown.\n\nReturn the requested numerical results and necessary scientific qualifications, including useful partial results. Distinguish missing source information from unimplemented calculations. Keep conditional scenarios, supported physical corrections and standardized comparisons separately identified. Target correspondence, final annotation credit and continuation decisions retain their existing owners."
